        "summary": "Dc susceptibility of dried 1·4H2O shows χMT decreasing from 128.5 cm3 K mol−1 at 300 K to 83.4 cm3 K mol−1 at 5.0 K, attributed to DyIII Stark-sublevel depopulation and NiII···DyIII antiferromagnetic interactions. Significant paramagnetism remains at 1.8 K (ac in-phase χMT ≈ 55 cm3 K mol−1). Frequency-dependent ac out-of-phase signals below 3 K, with maxima below 1.8 K, indicate slow magnetization relaxation and possible SMM behavior with a small barrier.",
